 In Memoriam: Bill Draper 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 William Draper III

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 William Draper III , a pioneer of Silicon Valley venture capital, has died at the age of 98.

 After college and military service, Draper and his father founded the West Coast's first venture capital firm. He later partnered with Pitch Johnson to form Sutter Hill Ventures and then, following a second career in public service, would found Draper International. He also is the father of venture capitalist Tim Draper and grandfather of venture capitalist Jesse Draper. What Jesse Draper wrote , in part: "What he did and helped create in Silicon Valley is immeasurable, but whenever he was given credit, he would pass it off to Leland Stanford ... Family came first, a lesson he taught us all ... He was at every major event in my life, cheering and standing with a hand in the air, from my high school graduation to college graduation..." 

 "He was fiercely competitive when it came to chess, tennis, and just about any other game. He had a bowl of chocolate ice cream every day and often declared, 'Hot fudge sundaes all around!' I was lucky enough to say goodbye to him on my grandmother's birthday, the day before he passed, and to witness his final words with my aunt. Believe it or not, they were: 'Ice cream.'" 
 
